    text            : keyword and semantic search, enabling accurate data retrieval and improved decision-making. Intelligent Search has been designed for scalability, to ensure it can cater for large enterprise data sets. Anticipated benefits and primary use-cases include: • Prebuilt adapter enabling a modern Siebel Search UX powered by OpenSearch for enhanced productivity and usability. • Unified Search UX with object filters delivering an intuitive, user-friendly interface for fast data retrieval. • Integrated solution supporting keyword and semantic search across global business objects and file attachments to retrieve relevant results. • Enterprise-grade, scalable search handling vast amounts of information efficiently and reliably. AES 256 Data encryption is being migrated to AES 256 • Security Guide No Replacement encryption leveraging OpenSSL. This change • Install Guide Using OpenSSL applies to data stored in the Siebel Database, the Siebel Gateway Registry, and Siebel Server services. NOTE: Customers will require at least some minimal downtime for this encryption replacement. This applies to this Monthly Update (25.10), but if, for example, a customer is later updating from 24.9 to 25.12, the downtime required for this change will occur at that time. For more information on this, please see the following documentation: • For customers on traditional Siebel CRM architectures, please review My Oracle Support Alert Special Considerations for Updating Siebel from pre-25.10 to 25.10 or Later (Doc ID 3107936.1) • For customers who are on a Siebel CRM container deployment, please additionally review My Oracle Support Alert Special Considerations for Updating Siebel from pre-25.10 to 25.10 or Later When Running on Containers (Doc ID 3107887.1) Training on this feature is available on Oracle University.

