    text            : Category Migration Subcategory Synchronous Bug No 37937312 Data migrations can be synchronous or asynchronous. Those customers using Application Deployment Manager (ADM) as part of their migrations will find that synchronous migrations fail due to generated cookies that are incompatible with Tomcat 10.1 which rejects them. In 25.6 we updated Tomcat to version 10.1 since we have updated Java to Java 21 and must update the way cookies are generated during synchronous migrations. The previous version of Tomcat (9) allowed cookie headers to have commas “,” in them and now requires semicolons “;” instead.

  [ITEM 2] 26_5_update_logical_block_3180
    page            : 182
    confidence      : 0.74
    pattern         : pattern_002
    role sequence   : BODY
    source blocks   : 26_5_update_block_3260
    item evidence   :
      - structural_self_support: 0.70
      - boundary_isolation: 1.00
      - repetition_support: 1.00
      - content_density: 0.20
    text            : If you do not use ADM in your migrations you will be unaffected by this situation.

  [ITEM 3] 26_5_update_logical_block_3181
    page            : 182
    confidence      : 0.70
    pattern         : pattern_004
    role sequence   : PROMINENT
    source blocks   : 26_5_update_block_3261
    item evidence   :
      - structural_self_support: 0.70
      - boundary_isolation: 1.00
      - repetition_support: 1.00
      - content_density: 0.03
    text            : _Remediation_

  [ITEM 4] 26_5_update_logical_block_3182
    page            : 182
    confidence      : 0.77
    pattern         : pattern_002
    role sequence   : BODY
    source blocks   : 26_5_update_block_3262
    item evidence   :
      - structural_self_support: 0.70
      - boundary_isolation: 1.00
      - repetition_support: 1.00
      - content_density: 0.36
    text            : The workaround for this is to perform asynchronous migrations instead of synchronous migrations if you include ADM packages in your migrations.

